======================================================================
1. PURPOSE
======================================================================

This repository is intentionally made publicly accessible to establish,
identify, explain, document, and permit technical review of the public
architecture of the Veil Routing Protocol ("VRP").

The repository may describe architectural principles concerning,
among other things:

- logical session identity;
- transport independence;
- transport replacement;
- session continuity;
- session lifetime;
- canonical state;
- canonical admission;
- authority;
- historical execution;
- replay handling;
- duplicate handling;
- recovery;
- fail-closed behavior;
- evidence-oriented verification;
- integration boundaries;
- security objectives.

Public availability of this repository does not make the VRP project,
its protected implementation, or its non-public engineering material
open source.

Except for the limited permissions expressly granted by this license,
no copyright, patent, trademark, trade-secret, source-code,
implementation, commercialization, distribution, sublicensing,
certification, endorsement, or other intellectual-property rights
are granted merely by publication of this repository.

For avoidance of doubt:

    PUBLIC ACCESS != OPEN SOURCE

    PUBLIC ARCHITECTURE != PUBLIC CORE

    DISCLOSURE != IMPLEMENTATION LICENSE


